Random Number Generation

Var n= Math.random();

Output=0-0.999999999999999

N= n*6 +;   - Numbers between 0-6 (float)

N = Math.floor(n*6)+1; --- Print Integer Values 


CONDITIONALS

IF to evaluate one way, else must be used for the next ways.

Example.

If (track  ===  'clear'){
	goStraight();
	} Else {               -----------------> This is used for only 2 ways
	turnRight ();
	}
	
If there are more outputs use else if 
Ex.
if (randomNum >= 95 && randomNum < 100) {
    alert(nom1 + ' and ' + nom2 + ' have a love score of ' + randomNum + '% of compatibility, that is true love');
} else if (randomNum >= 70 && randomNum < 95) {
    alert(nom1 + ' and ' + nom2 + ' have a love score of ' + randomNum + '% of compatibility, that is good love, you can still work in it');
} else if (randomNum >= 50 && randomNum < 70) {
    alert(nom1 + ' and ' + nom2 + ' have a love score of ' + randomNum + '% of compatibility, that is okay love');
} else {
    alert(nom1 + ' and ' + nom2 + ' have a love score of ' + randomNum + '% of compatibility, there is no love');
}


Comparators and Equality

Syntaxis	Used for
===	Is Equal to
!==	Is not equal to
>	Is greater than
>=	Is equal or greater than
<	Is lesser than
<=	Is equal or lesser than
==	To check datatype
&&	And
||	Or
!	not

Typeof() ----------> syntaxis to check type of data



Arrays

Var array = ['uno', 'dos', 'tres']

Array.length  ------> It gives you the ammount of items in the array

Array.includes('specific_item') ------------> to track if the item matches the array

Var output = [];
Output.push(); -------------> to add an element to the last part of the array
Outpush.pop(); ----------> to eliminate an element of the last place of the array


